<title>USA: Atwood says Australian rig gets contract.</title>
<headline>Atwood says Australian rig gets contract.</headline>
<dateline>HOUSTON 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Atwood Oceanics Inc said on Thursday that its Australian subsidiary received a contract for the use of the Atwood Southern Cross to drill a 175 days program off the coast of Australia.</p>
<p>The company said the rig will further enhance the company's 1998 operating result. The rig will undergo refurbishment and upgrade at a cost of $25 million.</p>
<p>The company said that it is optimistic that additional contract opportunities will be identified for the Atwood Southern Cross.</p>
<p>-- ((New York newsdesk 212-859-1611))</p>
</text>
